On Wed, 9 Sep 1998, Doug Rabson wrote:

> For anyone experimenting with FreeBSD/alpha at the moment, please avoid
> trying to use shared libraries for the next couple of days and keep your
> systems static.  The nice folks at Cygnus have managed to change the
> shared object format in such a way that shared executables and libs linked
> eith binutils-2.8.1 are totally incompatible with those linked with
> binutils-2.9.1.
> 
> Since we haven't released anything yet, I will only be supporting the
> 2.9.1 format in rtld but I have some more testing to do before I can
> commit that so stay static for the next few days.
> 
> For any of the NetBSD folks reading this list, be warned that you will get
> grief from binutils if/when you upgrade your toolchain to binutils-2.9.1.
> To be specific, the PLT format has changed and you will probably need two
> versions of _rtld_bind_start for the new and old formats :-(.

It should now be safe to build shared libs and dynamic executables on
alpha.  Make sure rtld-elf is up to date before trying to run any shared
executables.

