Justin and I discovered that write caching was turned off on the 2gig
DEC OEM Barracudas that came with the Miata.  Enabling write caching
improved performance a good bit.

To check for that, do this:

subway# camcontrol modepage -n da -u 0 -m 8
IC:  0 
ABPF:  0 
CAP:  0 
DISC:  1 
SIZE:  0 
WCE:  0 
MF:  0 
RCD:  0 
Demand Retention Priority:  0 
Write Retention Priority:  0 
Disable Pre-fetch Transfer Length:  65535 
Minimum Pre-fetch:  0 
Maximum Pre-fetch:  65535 
Maximum Pre-fetch Ceiling:  65535 

Notice that WCE is set to 0.  Set it to 1 to enable write caching.  You can
edit the mode page like this:

camcontrol modepage -n da -u 0 -m 8 -P 3 -e


Ken
